OBSERVATIONS (not FAILs; out of LT6's scope)
1. Pre-existing on master: the base-layout inline theme bootstrap
   (web/templates/layouts/base.html, `localStorage.getItem('theme')`) throws an
   uncaught error when Storage access is blocked. Identical message and stack
   on the master server :8104. Backlog candidate: wrap it in try/catch.
2. The Go test asserts `hx-trigger="load"` appears anywhere in the rendered
   output rather than on #chart-trends specifically. Non-vacuous today (M6
   proves it), but a second hx-trigger="load" elsewhere in insights-content
   would silently weaken it.
3. The Go test's ARIA pairing is set-wise (every aria-controls is SOME panel id,
   every aria-labelledby is SOME tab id); a transposed pair would pass it. The
   actual per-key pairing was verified separately against the served markup (all
   five tab-k -> panel-k) and behaviourally (activating tab k shows only panel
   k, for all five keys, in probe1 and probe5).
